\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The exact standard-cat boundary for \(1\le n\le 12\). Primitive divisors certify the ordinary positive cases. Period ten is instead repaired by the modulo-five Jordan calculation: twenty points form two primitive ten-cycles. The determinant supports and complete profiles \(p=2:\{3:3\}\), \(p=3:\{4:8\}\), and \(p=5:\{2:4,10:20\}\) exclude precisely \(1,6,12\).}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cat-boundary}{{2}{6}{The exact standard-cat boundary for \(1\le n\le 12\). Primitive divisors certify the ordinary positive cases. Period ten is instead repaired by the modulo-five Jordan calculation: twenty points form two primitive ten-cycles. The determinant supports and complete profiles \(p=2:\{3:3\}\), \(p=3:\{4:8\}\), and \(p=5:\{2:4,10:20\}\) exclude precisely \(1,6,12\)}{figure.2}{}}
\newlabel{thm:cat}{{4.2}{6}{Sharp standard-cat classification}{theorem.4.2}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {5}Capacity is not specificity}{7}{section.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:clock}{{5}{7}{Capacity is not specificity}{section.5}{}}
\newlabel{thm:clock}{{5.1}{7}{Torsion-order capacity and regularity obstruction}{theorem.5.1}{}}
\newlabel{eq:per-tor}{{15}{7}{Torsion-order capacity and regularity obstruction}{equation.5.15}{}}
\newlabel{eq:clock-unbounded}{{18}{7}{Capacity is not specificity}{equation.5.18}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Capacity versus specificity of the torsion-order clock. The witnesses \(x_m=(1/m,0)\) realize prime and composite orders by the same construction. At a frozen order-18 point, coprime perturbation denominators \(19,55,127\) give exact orders \(342,990,2286\), illustrating the general proof of local unboundedness. On an order-five, period-ten carrier, \(S_{10}L=10\qopname  \relax o{log}5\) and repetitions scale this sum, whereas \(A^{10}=\left (\begin  {smallmatrix}10946&6765\\6765&4181 \end  {smallmatrix}\right )\) and its characteristic polynomial \(X^2-15127X+1\) depend on the period but not on torsion order.}}{8}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:capacity-specificity}{{3}{8}{Capacity versus specificity of the torsion-order clock. The witnesses \(x_m=(1/m,0)\) realize prime and composite orders by the same construction. At a frozen order-18 point, coprime perturbation denominators \(19,55,127\) give exact orders \(342,990,2286\), illustrating the general proof of local unboundedness. On an order-five, period-ten carrier, \(S_{10}L=10\log 5\) and repetitions scale this sum, whereas \(A^{10}=\left (\begin {smallmatrix}10946&6765\\6765&4181 \end {smallmatrix}\right )\) and its characteristic polynomial \(X^2-15127X+1\) depend on the period but not on torsion order}{figure.3}{}}
